The `&` operator in Rust performs bitwise AND operation. When we apply this operator on an even number and 1, the result will be zero because all the rightmost bits will be cleared. On the other hand, when we apply this operator on an odd number and 1, the result won't be zero since at least one rightmost bit will be set. This implementation has a better performance than the JavaScript version with multiple `if` statements.

