        // Calculate duration between the two dates/times considering time zones
        Duration duration = Duration.between(start, end);

        // Print the calculated duration
        System.out.println("Duration: " + duration);
    }
}
```

In this example, `ZoneId.of("Europe/London")` sets the starting date/time in London's time zone, and `ZoneId.of("America/New_York")` sets the ending date/time in New York's time zone. You can replace these time zones with any other desired time zones. This program uses the `Duration` class from the `java.time` package to calculate the duration between the two dates/times, taking into account the time zone differences. The result is printed to the console as a `Duration` object, which includes fields such as hours, minutes, seconds, and nanoseconds.

